From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve workqueue parallelism on P-only AMP topologies

The AMP scheduler already runs every QoS on the performance cluster
when the efficiency cluster is absent. Report the matching parallelism
to the workqueue admission checks so Utility and Background requests
can receive workers on homogeneous virtual machines.

---
 osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
@@ -486,6 +486,11 @@ sched_amp_qos_max_parallelism(int qos, uint64_t options)
 		return (options & QOS_PARALLELISM_CLUSTER_SHARED_RESOURCE) ? pcluster_count : pcount;
 	}
 
+	/* A P-only topology schedules every QoS on the P cluster. */
+	if (ecount == 0) {
+		return (options & QOS_PARALLELISM_CLUSTER_SHARED_RESOURCE) ? pcluster_count : pcount;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * The default AMP scheduler policy is to run utility and by
 	 * threads on E-Cores only.  Run-time policy adjustment unlocks
